                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The idea behind the game is nice - you are a light in maze and can only see a small part of the maze. The execution however leaves everything to be desired:\n\n- the game is highly unoptimized and runs like garbage\n- there is no settings menu except the default Unity one they didn't even bother to change\n- only mouse control\n- no level select\n- after the first few levels the mazes get ridiculously big and highly tedious and unenjoyable.\n\nI lasted 25 levels before I called it quits because I just couldn't take any more of it. I have no idea how many there are in total because the game won't actually tell you anywhere and I don't think there is probably maybe people if any that actually got this far.\n\nThis feels like the dev spent about 30 minutes in Unity and now asks way too much more for what this is for this game (3,29€).",
